/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414529 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414529 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186414518 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414529 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "87ba22fc-b228-58c2-a360-feff99b2bf89" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414532 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186414500 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414532 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186414501 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414532 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186414503 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414532 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186414504 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414532 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186414517 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414532 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414532 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414532 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186414501 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414532 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c0a52ada-8c54-5615-81ca-fa8f0f0a0820" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414541 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186414524 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414541 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186414526 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414541 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186414529 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414541 #edb/ref 1069 "q-333011" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414541 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414541 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+\\begin{bmatrix}-3{t}^{2}+4t-4 \\\\ -{t}^{2}-2t+1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe complementary solution to this system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}t+2 \\\\ t+1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThen, the general solution of the system is\n\n| $x(t)={x}_{c}(t)+\\,\\,$ |  | $1$ |  | $\\,\\,{t}^{2}+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  | $\\,\\,t+\\,\\,$ |  | $1$ |  | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  | $2$ |  |  | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |  |  |" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186414541 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0f0ab548-1239-59aa-8a8e-1144624f4ff6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414541 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-3{t}^{2}+4t-4 \\\\ -{t}^{2}-2t+1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is polynomial of degree $2.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also polynomial of degree $2,$ i.e.\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1}{t}^{2}+{b}_{1}t+{c}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}{t}^{2}+{b}_{2}t+{c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}{t}^{2}+\\begin{bmatrix}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}t+\\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{c}_{1},{c}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the derivative of ${x}_{p}$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2{a}_{1}t+{b}_{1} \\\\ 2{a}_{2}t+{b}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2{a}_{1} \\\\ 2{a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}t+\\begin{bmatrix}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the unknown constants, we substitute ${x}_{p}$ and ${x}_{p}^{′}$ into our system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}2{a}_{1} \\\\ 2{a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}t+\\begin{bmatrix}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}(\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}{t}^{2}+\\begin{bmatrix}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}t+\\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix})+\\begin{bmatrix}-3{t}^{2}+4t-4 \\\\ -{t}^{2}-2t+1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}2{a}_{1}t+{b}_{1} \\\\ 2{a}_{2}t+{b}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2({a}_{1}{t}^{2}+{b}_{1}t+{c}_{1})-({a}_{2}{t}^{2}+{b}_{2}t+{c}_{2}) \\\\ {a}_{1}{t}^{2}+{b}_{1}t+{c}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-3{t}^{2}+4t-4 \\\\ -{t}^{2}-2t+1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}0{t}^{2}+2{a}_{1}t+{b}_{1} \\\\ 0{t}^{2}+2{a}_{2}t+{b}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}(2{a}_{1}-{a}_{2}-3){t}^{2}+(2{b}_{1}-{b}_{2}+4)t+(2{c}_{1}-{c}_{2}-4) \\\\ ({a}_{1}-1){t}^{2}+({b}_{1}-2)t+({c}_{1}+1)\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}-{a}_{2}-3 &=0 \\\\ 2{b}_{1}-{b}_{2}+4 &=2{a}_{1} \\\\ 2{c}_{1}-{c}_{2}-4 &={b}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1}-1 &=0 \\\\ {b}_{1}-2 &=2{a}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{1}+1 &={b}_{2}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSolving the fourth equation and then substituting the corresponding values ​​into the first and fifth equations to solve for ${a}_{2}$ and ${b}_{2},$ we get \n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=1,\\,{a}_{2}=-1,\\,{b}_{1}=0.\n$$\n\n \n\nWe substitute these into the second equation to solve for ${b}_{2},$ and then into the sixth and third equations to solve for ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$ We finally get\n\n$$\n{b}_{2}=2,\\,{c}_{1}=-1,\\,{c}_{2}=-2.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}{t}^{2}+1 \\\\ -\\,{t}^{2}+2t-2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}{t}^{2}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}t+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186414542 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186414532 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414542 #edb/ref 1069 "q-332740" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414542 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414542 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+{e}^{6t}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nA complementary solution to this system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{2t}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}{e}^{2t}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{bmatrix},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThen, the general solution of the system can be written as \n$x(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t),$\nwhere ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution. Determine the form of the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t).$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186414542 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "47fd4ff4-6ba7-5ef0-9848-b6ea043ad002" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414542 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere (\\mathbf{x}_c(t)) is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n\n$$\n{e}^{6t}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is exponential. Therefore, we assume that the particular solution has the same exponential factor, i.e.\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)={e}^{6t}\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1},{a}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186428951 #edb/ref 1030 0.5 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186428951 #edb/ref 1032 "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account differential: 1 rises / 2 eligible passed source activities = 0.500000; nearest selected fraction = 1/2. Crossing activity numbers [2]; waits [2]. Separate account estimates: differential=1/2 (1/2). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: True. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage; a multi-band rise counts once. This does not interpre